      "body": "Off Leash update 17 November 2026\n\nUKRAINE\n•So much for peace talks. Russia launched its annual winter bombing campaign weeks earlier than expected this year, pounding Ukraine’s energy infrastructure with increasing intensity. Pres. Zelensky believes the Kremlin “want[s] to come to the table holding our energy system hostage.”\n•Ukraine isn’t exactly waiting idle at the negotiating table, either. It has launched massive drone attacks on Russia each of the past two nights. Moscow claimed it downed 1,336 Ukrainian drones overnight Monday, which was the most in a single night since the war began…until last night, when Russia said it intercepted 1,441 more drones from Ukraine.\n•Ukraine also attacked the Kerch Bridge, which Russia uses to supply occupied Crimea. Ukraine considers the bridge illegal and has repeatedly sought to destroy it. It may have succeeded this time: unverified reports suggest a central arch span collapsed. [Moscow claimed the damage to the bridge was insignificant, but its own governor in Crimea acknowledged the bridge is currently out of commission.]\n\nIRAN\n•Bahrain convicted 69 Shia clerics and scholars of conspiring with Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps to “change the system of [Bahrain’s] government by force and unlawful means through incitement to commit terrorist acts, acts of rioting and sabotage.”\n\n007\n•British actor Robert Pattinson was announced as the seventh James Bond. His first Bond movie – which hasn’t been announced yet – will also be the first under the creative control of Amazon.",
